    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Meningioma, CNS WHO grade 1, after resection (D32.0)</content>. No residual or recurrent tumor at three months. [S]<list><item>Next MRI one year after surgery, then yearly to five years.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Focal epilepsy on levetiracetam (G40.109)</content>. Seizure-free for sixteen weeks with resolving side effects. PHQ-9 6 and GAD-7 5. Her state&apos;s seizure-free requirement of three months is met, and the neurosurgeon has cleared her to drive. [S]<list><item>Continue levetiracetam 500 mg twice a day; at one year after surgery, an EEG and a discussion of tapering.</item><item>She may drive again; no driving for at least three months after any seizure, and never after a missed dose with symptoms.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Surveillance MRI with gadolinium</td><td>Three months after resection, then yearly for five years, then every two years</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Five days ago: no residual or recurrent tumor; reviewed with her today</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Seizure diary, triggers (sleep loss, alcohol, missed doses), and seizure first aid</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No seizures for sixteen weeks; no missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9, with a question about irritability on levetiracetam</td><td>Every visit while on levetiracetam and during cancer treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>6, improving; irritability faded</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>GAD-7</td><td>Every visit during the diagnostic and treatment phase</td><td>Completed today</td><td>5, mild, done as the corrective action recorded at the last visit</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Levetiracetam tolerability</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Irritability resolved; no sleepiness or dizziness</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Driving</td><td>After the state&apos;s seizure-free period and surgical clearance</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Three months seizure-free and cleared by neurosurgery; may drive</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Occupational therapy</td><td>Until hand function recovers</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Course finished; full function</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>A diagnosis within two weeks, explained in plain words with the images and reports. Outcome by 2026-03-17: MRI and EEG within a week; diagnosis explained at two weeks with the images [S]</item><item>No further seizures. In progress; target 2027-04-07 [S]</item><item>Full use of the right hand and return to writing every morning. In progress; target 2026-09-29 [S]</item><item>Decide on treatment herself after hearing the options, benefits, and harms. Outcome by 2026-03-17: Chose resection after observation and radiosurgery were explained [S]</item><item>Mood and grief supported: PHQ-9 below 5 and a counselor available. In progress; target 2026-09-29 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: EANO guideline on the diagnosis and management of meningiomas. Goldbrunner R, et al. Neuro Oncol 2021;23(11):1821-1834 (2021); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Central Nervous System Cancers, Version 2.2025 (2025); Evidence-based guideline: Management of an unprovoked first seizure in adults. Krumholz A, et al. Neurology 2015;84(16):1705-1713 (2015); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (depression screening and PHQ-9 follow-up) (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Review in about twelve weeks; counselor as she wishes; MRI one year after surgery. Next scheduled visit 2026-09-29: six-month review after resection: seizures, mood, and writing. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
